# isoloom targets
✗ cloud-vm (no cloud can run it (aws, azure: machine `dc01`: Windows steps are .ps1 scripts; gcp: machine `dc01`: Windows on GCP comes later; digitalocean: DigitalOcean cloud-vm takes one machine on one network: a droplet joins one VPC, at a private address DigitalOcean picks, so other machines couldn't reach it at its spec address; linode: machine `web01` is on several networks: a Linode instance has one VPC interface; oci: Oracle Cloud cloud-vm is Linux only so far))

# isoloom generate --target cloud-vm (exit 1)
· cloud-vm: no cloud can run it (aws, azure: machine `dc01`: Windows steps are .ps1 scripts; gcp: machine `dc01`: Windows on GCP comes later; digitalocean: DigitalOcean cloud-vm takes one machine on one network: a droplet joins one VPC, at a private address DigitalOcean picks, so other machines couldn't reach it at its spec address; linode: machine `web01` is on several networks: a Linode instance has one VPC interface; oci: Oracle Cloud cloud-vm is Linux only so far)
